      "writtenOn": "2022-03-22T22:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s significant, I\u0027m getting 54956 B vs 57244 B with logging so more than 2kB. Haven\u0027t looked into where that space goes but stack plus buffer plus strdup buffers... I would suggest converting the prints you really want to CPRINT, we should rethink what to do with logging separately. The default async logging is cool but may not be for us, but we may consider syncronous or dictionary logging, or even a custom backend.",
      "parentUuid": "ce37e44c_7d1c1c0f",
      "revId": "42d999f9d42c3875386354b6fead89e1768eae16",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6043be4_d3fc2c2e",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-22T23:02:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So perhaps leave it on for Nivviks, since we are not getting a RAM issue there.\nAs Peter says, just about all the Nissa code uses logging as opposed to CPRINT, and turning it off completely at this stage may hamper our bring-up.\n\nLonger term, we do need to figure out what to do about logging.\nIt would be great if we can determine where the space is going, and maybe implement a custom slimmed down backend that would allow us to continue using the API.",
      "parentUuid": "70134c52_57bb1c19",
      "revId": "42d999f9d42c3875386354b6fead89e1768eae16",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9bb91ee7_d63d6595",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-22T23:08:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like we could reduce `LOG_STRDUP_MAX_STRING` and `LOG_STRDUP_BUF_COUNT`, possibly even to 0 for the latter since I don\u0027t think we ever expect to log strings that get constructed dynamically. Turning off `LOG_RUNTIME_FILTERING` might also provide some savings without disabling logging completely.",
      "parentUuid": "a6043be4_d3fc2c2e",
      "revId": "42d999f9d42c3875386354b6fead89e1768eae16",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d88c9690_b265c2b4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1478788
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-23T11:31:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dynamic strings are used all over the main RTOS code... I don\u0027t quite see the point to keep deferred logging enabled and then pin down all its configuration to the point of consciously breaking some of its features.\n\nWould LOG_MODE_MINIMAL work for you? That has only flash space implications, and even then you could shut off individual module logs and only keep the one you care about.\n\nIf it works well and you find it helpful we may consider looking more into it and changing the project default (which is probably worth doing for the thread name you changed recently as well).\n\n(updated this patch for minimal logging)",
      "parentUuid": "9bb91ee7_d63d6595",
      "revId": "42d999f9d42c3875386354b6fead89e1768eae16",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5100408_8fc0b389",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-23T12:08:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The underlying issue is that Nereid (IT81302) is having a serious RAM crunch, and effectively we\u0027re just playing whack-a-mole. We get savings where we can.\nA core issue is that the stack usage for RISC-V seems to be about 20% higher than ARM, and with the number of tasks we have (~16?), the margins are very tight.\nAs an ongoing task, we\u0027re trying to find out where most of the RAM usage is.\nHowever, I worry that we\u0027re rapidly hitting diminishing returns.",
      "parentUuid": "d88c9690_b265c2b4",
      "revId": "42d999f9d42c3875386354b6fead89e1768eae16",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
